<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85402" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολυ-σχῐδής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχίζω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>split into many parts,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁπλῷ τρόπῳ καὶ μὴ
			πολυσχιδέϊ</span> by a single and not <i>a splintered
				fracture,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				24
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λώβῃσι πολυσχιδέεσσι
			λυθέντα,</span> of a wreck, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				4.409
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>much-cloven,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσχιδής,</span> of certain figs, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				930b33
			</span></i>; of a deer's antlers, <i>branching,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HA</u>
				517a24
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PA</u>
				663a10
			</span></i>; of the lungs, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HA</u>
				495b1
			</span></i>; of leaves, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				3.12.5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καυλοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					2.185
				</span></i>
			; of a mountain range, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				11.12.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτραποί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.969b
				</span></i>
			; of the Nile, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				2.85
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Or.</u>
				61.18
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of the hand,
				<i>cloven into fingers,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>PA</u>
				687b7
			</span></i>; of the foot, <i>into toes,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				690b6
			</span></i>: hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ π.</span>
			<i>animals that have toes,</i> not hoofs, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HA</u>
				497b20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				499b7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				502b34
			</span></i>; esp. of birds, ib.<i><span class="en">
				504a6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> generally,
				<i>much divided,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνῶμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					7.349
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμφασις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Iamb.
					<u>VP</u>
					29.161
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψεῦδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Protr.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ́;</span>”
				<i>complex,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ammon.
					<u>in Cat.</u>
					66.9
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-δῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.31
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
